    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    n = data                                          # index of the Fibonacci number we want\n    def mat_mult(a, b):                                # multiply two 2x2 matrices\n        return [                                       # standard row-by-column matrix product\n            a[0]*b[0] + a[1]*b[2], a[0]*b[1] + a[1]*b[3],  # top row of the result\n            a[2]*b[0] + a[3]*b[2], a[2]*b[1] + a[3]*b[3],  # bottom row of the result\n        ]\n    result = [1, 0, 0, 1]                              # identity matrix (accumulates the power)\n    base = [1, 1, 1, 0]                                # the Fibonacci Q-matrix [[1,1],[1,0]]\n    e = n                                              # exponent to apply via binary exponentiation\n    while e > 0:                                        # process each bit of the exponent\n        if e & 1:                                       # if the current low bit is set\n            result = mat_mult(result, base)             # fold the current base power into the result\n        base = mat_mult(base, base)                     # square the base for the next bit\n        e >>= 1                                         # shift to the next exponent bit\n    return result[1]                                    # entry [0][1] of Q^n equals F(n)",
