    "type": "python",
    "question": "Write `solve(data)` where `data` is `[nums, k]`. Return the maximum sum of any contiguous subarray of exactly length k, using a fixed-size sliding window in O(N) time (slide by subtracting the element leaving and adding the one entering). If len(nums) < k, return None.",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, k = data[0], data[1]\n    # TODO: max sum of any window of size k, O(N)\n    return None",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, k = data[0], data[1]                    # unpack the array and the window length\n    if len(nums) < k:                               # window cannot fit\n        return None                                # signal that no valid window exists\n    window = sum(nums[:k])                          # sum of the very first window of size k\n    best = window                                   # best window sum seen so far\n    for i in range(k, len(nums)):                   # slide the window one step at a time\n        window += nums[i] - nums[i - k]             # add the entering element, drop the leaving element\n        if window > best:                           # update the running maximum\n            best = window                           # record the larger window sum\n    return best                                     # maximum window sum overall",
