    "question": "Simulate dispatching tasks to `w` workers using round-robin scheduling. `data` is a list `[durations, w]` where `durations` is a list of positive integers (task cost, in submission order) and `w` is the number of workers. Task i goes to worker (i mod w); each worker runs its tasks sequentially. Write `solve(data)` that returns the makespan: the finish time of the busiest worker (the max total load across workers). NOTE: No real threads are used; we compute the deterministic outcome of the schedule.",
