    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    durations, w = data[0], data[1]              # unpack task costs and worker count\n    if w <= 0:                                   # no workers means nothing can run\n        return 0                                 # makespan is zero\n    loads = [0] * w                              # per-worker accumulated busy time\n    for i, d in enumerate(durations):            # dispatch tasks in submission order\n        worker = i % w                           # round-robin: task i -> worker i mod w\n        loads[worker] += d                       # that worker runs the task sequentially\n    return max(loads) if loads else 0            # makespan = finish time of the busiest worker",
