    "title": "Two Sum: Count All Distinct Value Pairs",
    "question": "Given a list of integers and a target, count the number of DISTINCT value pairs (unordered) that sum to the target. `data` is a list `[nums, target]`. A pair is identified by its two values (not indices); each distinct value-pair is counted once. Write `solve(data)` that returns the count.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, target = data[0], data[1]\n    # Return the number of distinct value pairs summing to target\n    return 0",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, target = data[0], data[1]              # unpack the numbers and target sum\n    seen = set()                                 # distinct values encountered so far\n    pairs = set()                                # distinct value-pairs that sum to target\n    for x in nums:                               # scan each number once\n        complement = target - x                  # the value needed to reach the target\n        if complement in seen:                   # a matching partner was already seen\n            pairs.add((min(x, complement), max(x, complement)))  # store the pair canonically (sorted)\n        seen.add(x)                              # remember this value for future complements\n    return len(pairs)                            # number of distinct value pairs",
