    "title": "Large File Processing: Top-K Frequent Words",
    "question": "Simulate scanning a large text file. You are given `data` = [words, k] where `words` is a list of lowercase word strings and `k` is an integer. Write `solve(data)` that returns the top-k most frequent words as a list of [word, count] pairs, sorted by count descending, breaking ties by word ascending. Return at most k pairs.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef solve(data):\n    words, k = data[0], data[1]\n    # Return top-k [word, count] pairs by count desc, then word asc\n    return []",
    "solutionCode": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef solve(data):\n    words, k = data[0], data[1]                 # unpack the word list and k\n    counts = Counter(words)                      # tally frequency of each word in one pass\n    # sort by count descending, then word ascending to break ties deterministically\n    ordered = sorted(counts.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1], kv[0]))\n    top = ordered[:k]                            # take only the first k entries\n    return [[word, cnt] for word, cnt in top]    # format as [word, count] pairs",
