    "id": "py-c-52",
    "topicId": "python-topic-52",
    "category": "python",
    "title": "LRU Cache: Simulate Access Sequence",
    "question": "Simulate an LRU cache of fixed capacity. You are given `data` = [capacity, keys] where `keys` is a list of integer key accesses in order. Each access inserts the key (or refreshes it if present). When inserting a new key over capacity, evict the least-recently-used key first. Write `solve(data)` that returns the list of keys remaining in the cache, ordered from least-recently-used to most-recently-used.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "from collections import OrderedDict\n\ndef solve(data):\n    capacity, keys = data[0], data[1]\n    # Simulate LRU; return remaining keys LRU -> MRU\n    return []",
    "solutionCode": "from collections import OrderedDict\n\ndef solve(data):\n    capacity, keys = data[0], data[1]           # unpack capacity and the access sequence\n    cache = OrderedDict()                         # ordered map: front = LRU, back = MRU\n    for key in keys:                             # replay each access in order\n        if key in cache:                         # a hit refreshes the key's recency\n            cache.move_to_end(key)               # move it to the MRU end\n        else:                                    # a miss inserts a new key\n            cache[key] = True                    # add it (goes to the MRU end)\n            if len(cache) > capacity:            # over capacity after insert?\n                cache.popitem(last=False)        # evict the LRU item at the front\n    return list(cache.keys())                    # remaining keys from LRU to MRU",
    "testCases": [
      {
        "input": "[2, [1, 2, 3]]",
        "expected": "[2, 3]"
      },
      {
        "input": "[2, [1, 2, 1, 3]]",
        "expected": "[1, 3]"
      },
      {
        "input": "[0, [1, 2]]",
        "expected": "[]"
      }
    ],
    "hint": "1. Use OrderedDict; front is LRU, back is MRU.\n2. On hit, move_to_end; on miss, insert and evict if over capacity.\n3. Return keys front-to-back.",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "exampleInput": "[2, [1, 2, 3]]",
    "exampleOutput": "[2, 3]",
    "constraints": "Capacity 0..10^6, up to 10^6 accesses. Capacity 0 means nothing is ever retained.",
    "hints": [
      "OrderedDict.move_to_end and popitem(last=False) give O(1) LRU operations.",
      "Insert first, then evict, so a refreshed key is never wrongly dropped."
    ],
    "bruteForce": "Track recency timestamps in a list and scan for the min on eviction. Time Complexity: O(N) per eviction.",
    "optimized": "OrderedDict gives O(1) move/insert/evict. Time Complexity: O(N) overall.",
    "complexity": {
      "time": "O(N) over the access sequence",
      "space": "O(capacity)"
    },
