    "question": "Write `solve(data)` that takes a non-negative integer `data` = n and returns the number of trailing zeros in n! (n factorial) WITHOUT computing the factorial itself. Trailing zeros come from factors of 10 = 2*5, and 5s are the limiting factor.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    n = data\n    # Return the count of trailing zeros in n! without computing n!\n    return 0",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    n = data                                    # the input integer n\n    count = 0                                   # running total of factors of 5 in n!\n    power = 5                                    # successive powers of 5: 5, 25, 125, ...\n    while power <= n:                            # while this power of 5 still fits in n\n        count += n // power                     # add how many multiples of this power are <= n\n        power *= 5                               # move to the next higher power of 5\n    return count                                # total trailing zeros = total factors of 5",
