    "category": "python",
    "title": "Insert and Merge a New Interval",
    "question": "Given a list `[intervals, new_interval]` where `intervals` is a list of non-overlapping intervals [start, end] sorted by start, write `solve(data)` that inserts `new_interval` and merges any overlaps. Return the resulting sorted list of intervals.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    intervals, new_interval = data[0], data[1]\n    # Insert new_interval and merge overlaps; return sorted intervals\n    return []",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    intervals, new_interval = data[0], data[1]     # existing sorted intervals and the one to insert\n    result = []                                    # output list of merged intervals\n    i, n = 0, len(intervals)                       # index into intervals and its length\n    while i < n and intervals[i][1] < new_interval[0]:  # intervals ending before new starts: untouched\n        result.append(intervals[i])                # copy them straight through\n        i += 1                                      # advance\n    start, end = new_interval[0], new_interval[1]  # the merged interval we are building\n    while i < n and intervals[i][0] <= end:        # any interval overlapping the growing merge\n        start = min(start, intervals[i][0])        # extend left edge if needed\n        end = max(end, intervals[i][1])            # extend right edge if needed\n        i += 1                                      # absorb this interval\n    result.append([start, end])                    # push the fully merged interval\n    while i < n:                                    # remaining intervals start after the merge ends\n        result.append(intervals[i])                # copy them through unchanged\n        i += 1                                      # advance\n    return result                                   # final sorted, non-overlapping list",
