    "question": "Write `solve(data)` that takes a string and returns the length of the longest substring containing no repeated characters, using a sliding window. For example 'abcabcbb' -> 'abc' has length 3.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    # data: string\n    # Return length of longest substring with all-distinct characters\n    return 0",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    last_seen = {}                                 # char -> the most recent index we saw it\n    start = 0                                      # left edge of the current valid window\n    best = 0                                       # longest distinct-window length found so far\n    for i, ch in enumerate(data):                  # i is the right edge of the window\n        if ch in last_seen and last_seen[ch] >= start:  # this char repeats inside the window\n            start = last_seen[ch] + 1             # jump the left edge past the previous occurrence\n        last_seen[ch] = i                          # record/refresh where we last saw this char\n        best = max(best, i - start + 1)           # update the best window length\n    return best                                     # the answer",
