    "title": "Trailing Zeros in Factorial",
    "question": "Write `solve(data)` that takes a non-negative integer `n` and returns the number of trailing zeros in n! (n factorial) WITHOUT computing the factorial itself. For example, 5! = 120 has 1 trailing zero.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    n = data\n    # Return count of trailing zeros in n!\n    return 0",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    n = data                                          # the input integer\n    count = 0                                         # number of factor-5s (= trailing zeros)\n    power = 5                                          # current power of 5 we are counting\n    # Each trailing zero comes from a factor of 10 = 2*5; 5s are scarcer than 2s,\n    # so count multiples of 5, 25, 125, ... (Legendre's formula)\n    while power <= n:                                  # stop once 5^k exceeds n\n        count += n // power                            # add how many multiples of this power exist\n        power *= 5                                      # move to the next higher power of 5\n    return count                                       # total trailing zeros",
