    "question": "You are given data = [nums, k] where nums is a list of integers (may contain duplicates) and k is a positive integer. Write `solve(data)` that returns the kth LARGEST element by value (1-indexed: k=1 is the maximum). Duplicates count by position, so [3,3,1] with k=2 returns 3.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, k = data[0], data[1]\n    # Return the kth largest element\n    return None",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    nums, k = data[0], data[1]                         # the values and the rank we want\n    import heapq                                        # min-heap utilities\n    # Keep a min-heap of the k largest values seen so far.\n    # Its smallest element is exactly the kth largest overall.\n    heap = []                                           # the size-k min-heap\n    for num in nums:                                    # scan every value once\n        heapq.heappush(heap, num)                       # tentatively add the value\n        if len(heap) > k:                               # heap grew beyond k elements\n            heapq.heappop(heap)                         # drop the smallest, keeping top-k\n    return heap[0]                                      # heap root is the kth largest",
