    "question": "You are given data, a list of [start, end] intervals (integers, start <= end) that may overlap and may be unsorted. Write `solve(data)` that returns the total length of the number line covered by the union of all intervals (overlaps counted once). For [[1,4],[2,5],[7,9]] the covered length is 4 + 2 = 6.",
    "type": "python",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    # Return total covered length of the union of intervals\n    return 0",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    if not data:                                        # no intervals cover nothing\n        return 0\n    intervals = sorted(data)                            # sort by start (then end) ascending\n    total = 0                                            # accumulated covered length\n    cur_start, cur_end = intervals[0]                    # the interval currently being merged\n    for start, end in intervals[1:]:                     # walk the remaining intervals\n        if start <= cur_end:                             # overlaps or touches the current span\n            cur_end = max(cur_end, end)                  # extend the merged span if needed\n        else:                                            # a gap: the current span is final\n            total += cur_end - cur_start                 # add its length to the total\n            cur_start, cur_end = start, end              # begin a new merged span\n    total += cur_end - cur_start                         # add the final span's length\n    return total                                          # total union length",
