    "question": "From the `scores` table, assign each student a rank within their `class` based on `score` (highest score is rank 1). Students with equal scores share the same rank and the next rank is NOT skipped. Output `class`, `student`, `score`, and `class_rank`.",
    "type": "sql",
    "setupSql": "CREATE TABLE scores (id INT, class VARCHAR(50), student VARCHAR(255), score INT);\nINSERT INTO scores VALUES (1, 'A', 'Ann', 90), (2, 'A', 'Ben', 90), (3, 'A', 'Cay', 80), (4, 'A', 'Dee', 70), (5, 'B', 'Eli', 88), (6, 'B', 'Fia', 95), (7, 'B', 'Gus', 88);",
    "initialCode": "-- Write your SQL query here\nSELECT * FROM scores;",
    "solutionCode": "SELECT class, student, score,\n  -- DENSE_RANK gives tied scores the same rank without leaving gaps afterward\n  DENSE_RANK() OVER (\n    PARTITION BY class\n    ORDER BY score DESC\n  ) AS class_rank\nFROM scores\n-- deterministic ordering: by class, then rank, then student name to break ties\nORDER BY class, class_rank, student;",
    "hint": "1. Use DENSE_RANK (not RANK) so tied scores do not create gaps.\n2. PARTITION BY class restarts the ranking for each class.\n3. ORDER BY score DESC so the highest score is rank 1.",
