    "exampleOutput": "user_id | event_id | status\n100 | 3 | churned\n200 | 4 | new\n300 | 5 | active",
    "constraints": "Exactly one row per user. Break ts ties by larger event_id. Sort by user_id.",
    "hints": [
      "ROW_NUMBER guarantees a single winner per partition, unlike RANK.",
      "Add a secondary ORDER BY key to make tie-breaking deterministic."
    ],
    "bruteForce": "Correlated subquery selecting MAX(ts) then re-joining; messy with ties and slow.",
    "optimized": "Single ROW_NUMBER window with a deterministic ORDER BY, filtered to rn = 1.",
