    "title": "Custom Priority Sort With NULLs",
    "question": "Sort the `tickets` table so that open tickets ('open' before 'pending' before 'closed') come first, then by `priority` descending, and place tickets with a NULL `assignee` last within each group. Output `ticket_id`, `status`, `priority`, `assignee`.",
    "type": "sql",
    "setupSql": "CREATE TABLE tickets (ticket_id INTEGER, status TEXT, priority INTEGER, assignee TEXT);\nINSERT INTO tickets VALUES (1, 'closed', 3, 'amy'), (2, 'open', 5, NULL), (3, 'open', 5, 'ben'), (4, 'pending', 2, 'cara'), (5, 'open', 1, 'dee'), (6, 'pending', 4, NULL), (7, 'closed', 9, 'eli');",
    "initialCode": "-- Write your SQL query here\nSELECT * FROM tickets;",
    "solutionCode": "-- Order by a derived status rank, then priority, then NULL placement\nSELECT ticket_id, status, priority, assignee\nFROM tickets\nORDER BY\n  -- Map statuses to a sort rank so open < pending < closed\n  CASE status WHEN 'open' THEN 0 WHEN 'pending' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END,\n  -- Higher priority first\n  priority DESC,\n  -- NULL assignees sort after non-NULLs within the group\n  (assignee IS NULL),\n  -- Final tie-break for full determinism\n  ticket_id;",
    "hint": "1. Use CASE in ORDER BY to impose the custom status order.\n2. Sort priority DESC and push NULL assignees last with (assignee IS NULL).",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "exampleInput": "Table: tickets (ticket_id, status, priority, assignee)",
    "exampleOutput": "ticket_id | status | priority | assignee\n3 | open | 5 | ben\n2 | open | 5 | \n5 | open | 1 | dee\n6 | pending | 4 | \n4 | pending | 2 | cara\n7 | closed | 9 | eli\n1 | closed | 3 | amy",
    "constraints": "Status order open<pending<closed. priority descending. NULL assignee last per group. Tie-break by ticket_id.",
    "hints": [
      "A CASE expression in ORDER BY maps arbitrary categories to a numeric sort key.",
      "In SQLite, (col IS NULL) yields 0/1, so it can push NULLs to the end."
    ],
    "bruteForce": "N/A",
    "optimized": "Multi-key ORDER BY with a CASE-derived rank and a NULL-placement expression.",
    "complexity": {
      "time": "O(N log N)",
      "space": "O(N)"
    },
    "discussion": {
      "whyAsked": "Real reports need custom orderings beyond alphabetical, plus explicit NULL placement.",
      "mistakes": "Relying on default NULL ordering (engine-specific) or forgetting a final tie-break for determinism.",
      "followUps": [
        "How does NULLS LAST differ across databases?",
        "Why add ticket_id as the last sort key?"
      ]
    }
