    "initialCode": "-- Write your SQL query here\nSELECT * FROM orders;",
    "solutionCode": "-- Conditional aggregation pivots rows into quarter columns\nSELECT product,\n       SUM(CASE WHEN quarter = 'Q1' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) AS q1,  -- Q1 total\n       SUM(CASE WHEN quarter = 'Q2' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) AS q2,  -- Q2 total\n       SUM(CASE WHEN quarter = 'Q3' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) AS q3,  -- Q3 total\n       SUM(CASE WHEN quarter = 'Q4' THEN amount ELSE 0 END) AS q4   -- Q4 total\nFROM orders\nGROUP BY product\nORDER BY product;                                                  -- deterministic ordering",
    "hint": "1. SQLite has no PIVOT; use SUM(CASE WHEN quarter='Qn' THEN amount ELSE 0 END).\n2. Group by product so each product is a single row.",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "exampleInput": "Table: orders (product, quarter, amount)",
    "exampleOutput": "product | q1 | q2 | q3 | q4\nGadget | 0 | 200 | 0 | 120\nGizmo | 30 | 30 | 30 | 30\nWidget | 150 | 0 | 80 | 0",
    "constraints": "Quarters with no orders must show 0, not NULL. Sort by product.",
