    "id": "pyspark-c-46",
    "topicId": "pyspark-topic-46",
    "category": "pyspark",
    "title": "AQE: Coalesce Tiny Shuffle Partitions",
    "type": "pyspark",
    "question": "You are given data = {'partitions': [int, ...], 'min_size': int}. After a shuffle, AQE (Adaptive Query Execution) coalesces adjacent small partitions so each merged partition holds at least 'min_size' rows (the last group may be smaller). Walk partitions left to right, greedily accumulating into the current group until it reaches min_size, then start a new group. Write `solve(data)` returning the list of merged partition sizes. NOTE: emulate AQE's coalescePartitions logic in pure Python; inline comments show the concept.",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    # data: {'partitions': [int rowcounts], 'min_size': int}\n    # Greedily merge adjacent partitions until each group >= min_size; return merged sizes.\n    return []",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    # PySpark equivalent (conceptual):\n    #   spark.conf.set('spark.sql.adaptive.enabled', True)\n    #   spark.conf.set('spark.sql.adaptive.coalescePartitions.enabled', True)\n    #   # AQE reads actual post-shuffle partition sizes and merges tiny adjacent ones\n    #   # so downstream tasks aren't dominated by scheduling overhead on micro-partitions.\n    parts = data['partitions']                   # actual post-shuffle partition sizes (runtime statistics)\n    min_size = data['min_size']                   # target floor per coalesced partition\n    merged = []                                   # resulting coalesced partition sizes\n    current = 0                                   # rows accumulated in the in-progress group\n    started = False                               # whether the current group has any data yet\n    for size in parts:                            # walk partitions left to right (adjacency preserved)\n        current += size                           # fold this partition into the current group\n        started = True                            # mark group as non-empty\n        if current >= min_size:                   # group big enough -> seal it\n            merged.append(current)                # emit the coalesced partition\n            current = 0                           # reset accumulator\n            started = False                       # ready for a fresh group\n    if started:                                   # flush a trailing small group (allowed to be < min_size)\n        merged.append(current)\n    return merged                                 # fewer, healthier-sized partitions",
    "testCases": [
      {
        "input": "{'partitions':[10,10,10,10,10],'min_size':25}",
        "expected": "[30, 20]"
      },
      {
        "input": "{'partitions':[100,5,5],'min_size':50}",
        "expected": "[100, 10]"
      },
      {
        "input": "{'partitions':[5,5,5],'min_size':100}",
        "expected": "[15]"
      }
    ],
    "hint": "1. Greedily accumulate sizes until reaching min_size, then seal the group.\n2. Flush any trailing partial group at the end.",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "exampleInput": "{'partitions':[10,10,10,10,10],'min_size':25}",
    "exampleOutput": "[30, 20]",
    "constraints": "Sizes are non-negative integers; min_size >= 1.",
    "hints": [
      "AQE uses real runtime statistics gathered after the shuffle, not compile-time guesses.",
      "Too many tiny partitions waste scheduling time; AQE merges adjacent ones."
    ],
    "bruteForce": "Leave all shuffle partitions as-is (default 200), risking many micro-tasks. Time Complexity: O(P).",
    "optimized": "Single greedy pass coalescing adjacent partitions to a healthy size. Time Complexity: O(P).",
    "complexity": {
      "time": "O(P) for P partitions",
      "space": "O(P) for output"
    },
    "discussion": {
      "whyAsked": "AQE is a flagship Spark 3 feature; interviewers check you understand it adapts plans using runtime stats.",
      "mistakes": "Forgetting to flush the final group; assuming AQE reorders partitions (it only merges adjacent ones).",
      "followUps": [
        "What other optimizations does AQE perform (skew join handling, join strategy switch)?",
        "Why does AQE need to wait for a shuffle to finish before coalescing?"
      ]
    }
