    "question": "Reshaping for a tall/EAV model: given data = [{'entity': str, 'attrs': {attr: value}}, ...] (a wide record per entity), unpivot it into long rows of {'entity', 'attribute', 'value'}, one per attribute. Output rows sorted by (entity, attribute). Write `solve(data)` returning the list of long rows.",
    "initialCode": "def solve(data):\n    # data: list of {'entity': str, 'attrs': {attr: value}}\n    # Unpivot to long rows {entity, attribute, value}; sort by (entity, attribute).\n    return []",
    "solutionCode": "def solve(data):\n    rows = []                                          # accumulator for the long-format rows\n    for rec in data:                                   # each wide record holds many attributes\n        ent = rec[\"entity\"]                           # the entity this record describes\n        for attr, val in rec[\"attrs\"].items():        # explode each column into its own row (unpivot)\n            rows.append({\"entity\": ent, \"attribute\": attr, \"value\": val})  # one tall key-value row\n    rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r[\"entity\"], r[\"attribute\"]))  # deterministic order by entity then attribute\n    return rows                                        # normalized long/EAV representation",
